              <item>
               <widget class="QLabel" name="label_63">
                <property name="font">
                 <font>
                  <weight>75</weight>
                  <bold>true</bold>
                 </font>
                </property>
                <property name="text">
                 <string>INFO</string>
                </property>
               </widget>
              </item>
              <item>
               <widget class="QLabel" name="label_62">
                <property name="text">
                 <string>When the EffectShader is first applied to an object, the fill effect's alpha (opacity) will begin at zero and gradually increase to the Full Alpha Ratio, taking Alpha Fade-In Time seconds to do so. Once it reaches that point, it'll stay at that alpha for the Full Alpha Time duration. Afterwards, the alpha will gradually decrease to the Persistent Alpha Ratio, taking Alpha Fade-Out Time seconds to do so. By default, it'll stay at that alpha ratio until the EffectShader is removed. At that point, it'll fade out from its current opacity to zero over Alpha Fade-Out Time.

If the Persistent Alpha Ratio is greater than the Full Alpha Ratio, then the shader will instantly switch from the Full Alpha Ratio to the Persistent Alpha Ratio after the Full Alpha Time elapses.

The Alpha Pulse settings allow the alpha to fluctuate over the full lifetime of the shader, including during any fades. The Alpha Pulse Ratio defines the maximum ratio (multiplied by the Full or Persistent Alpha Ratio) by which the alpha can vary. The Alpha Pulse Frequency determines the length of the time period over which the alpha varies by ± the Alpha Pulse Ratio.</string>
                </property>
                <property name="alignment">
                 <set>Qt::AlignLeading|Qt::AlignLeft|Qt::AlignTop</set>
                </property>
                <property name="wordWrap">
                 <bool>true</bool>
                </property>
               </widget>
              </item>
              <item>
               <spacer name="verticalSpacer_5">
                <property name="orientation">
                 <enum>Qt::Vertical</enum>
                </property>
                <property name="sizeHint" stdset="0">
                 <size>
                  <width>20</width>
                  <height>0</height>
                 </size>
                </property>
               </spacer>
              </item>
             </layout>
            </widget>
           </item>
